<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Francesco Jacomoni</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1893">1893</a>–<a href="/years/1973">1973</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Francesco Jacomoni di San Savino</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Francesco Jacomoni was an Italian diplomat who served as minister in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tirana">Tirana</a> before the Italian invasion of 1939 and then as lieutenant-general of the King in Albania until 1943. In that office he held real power over the Albanian Kingdom in personal union with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, overseeing its fascist institutions and the merger of its army and foreign service into Italy's.</p></div>
